<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistani interbank rates seesaw in dull trade.</title>
<headline>Pakistani interbank rates seesaw in dull trade.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's interbank money market rates fluctuated widely on Thursday before closing in a single digit, dealers said.</p>
<p>The market opened amid mixed sentiment on another day of trading at the higher end of the spectrum, but later borrowers managed to bring rates into the single digit, at dealer at KASB &amp; Co said.</p>
<p>Lenders placed their amounts at around 7.00 and 8.00 percent, the dealer said.</p>
<p>-- Ibrahim Khan 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
